{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>All who approach, who approach, etc.</b> They were stirred up now and not before, even though this matter had already been said to them — as they said (Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:2:3): מַאן דְּנָכִית לֵיהּ חִוְיָא מֵחֶבְלָא — 'One whom a snake has bitten, [fears even] a rope,' etc."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The Aramaic proverb cited from Shir HaShirim Rabbah is translated in brackets to make the point intelligible; the citation identifier in the source matches the standard Shir HaShirim Rabbah 1:2 (3)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:47.233180116Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}